"pass on everything\" yields two years each and \"submit on everything\" yields four, and I'm also checking asymmetric policies where one copy's observation triggers a submit and the other's triggers a pass.\n\nI'm checking whether the asymmetric split beats pass-on-everything once I average over not knowing which copy I am: a 50/50 mix gives about 2.5 years, worse than the 2 from passing on every input. So passing on all inputs comes out best. I'm also noting the caveat that the other copy counts as subjunctively dependent under the setup, and concluding that the answer is to pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a prisoner's dilemma between two copies of the same agent, so I'm applying the policy-level framing: their outputs are determined by one shared policy that maps what each observes to an action. Comparing symmetric policies, \"pass on everything\" yields two years each and \"submit on everything\" yields four, and I'm also checking asymmetric policies where one copy's observation triggers a submit and the other's triggers a pass.\n\nI'm checking whether the asymmetric split beats pass-on-everything once I average over not knowing which copy I am: a 50/50 mix gives about 2.5 years, worse than the 2 from passing on every input. So passing on all inputs comes out best. I'm also noting the caveat that the other copy counts as subjunctively dependent under the setup, and concluding that the answer is to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9942,"completion_tokens":856,"total_tokens":10798,"cost":0.056888,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.056888,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039768,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01712},"completion_to